  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "IB SL statistics covers descriptive statistics, probability laws, distributions, and correlation — with extensive use of the GDC for computations and hypothesis tests (AI SL).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Descriptive statistics",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\[\\bar{x}=\\frac{\\sum f_ix_i}{\\sum f_i}\\quad(\\text{mean from frequency table}),\\quad IQR=Q_3-Q_1.\\]<p>A value is an outlier if \\(x&lt;Q_1-1.5\\,IQR\\) or \\(x&gt;Q_3+1.5\\,IQR.\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Probability",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\[P(A\\cup B)=P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B),\\quad P(A\\mid B)=\\frac{P(A\\cap B)}{P(B)}.\\]<p>Independent: \\(P(A\\cap B)=P(A)\\cdot P(B).\\) Mutually exclusive: \\(P(A\\cap B)=0.\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Distributions",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p><strong>Binomial</strong> \\(X\\sim B(n,p)\\): \\(P(X=k)=\\binom{n}{k}p^k(1-p)^{n-k},\\;\\mu=np,\\;\\sigma^2=np(1-p).\\)</p><p><strong>Normal</strong> \\(X\\sim N(\\mu,\\sigma^2)\\): \\(z=\\dfrac{x-\\mu}{\\sigma}.\\) Use GDC: <code>normalcdf</code>, <code>invNorm</code>.</p><p><strong>Bivariate (AI SL):</strong> Pearson's correlation \\(r\\); LSRL \\(\\hat{y}=ax+b\\). Use GDC for linear regression.</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● \\(\\chi^2\\) test for independence (AI SL)",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\[\\chi^2_{\\text{calc}}=\\sum\\frac{(f_o-f_e)^2}{f_e},\\quad f_e=\\frac{\\text{row total}\\times\\text{col total}}{\\text{grand total}}.\\]<p>Reject \\(H_0\\) (independence) if \\(\\chi^2_{\\text{calc}}&gt;\\chi^2_{\\text{crit}}\\) or \\(p&lt;\\) significance level.</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "workedExampleCard",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example 4.1",
          "ar": null
        },
        "problem": {
          "en": "\\(X\\sim B(12,0.35).\\) Find \\(P(X\\le4)\\) using GDC, and find \\(\\mu\\) and \\(\\sigma.\\)",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p>GDC: <code>binomcdf</code>(12, 0.35, 4) \\(\\approx0.583.\\)</p><p>\\(\\mu=12(0.35)=4.2.\\quad\\sigma=\\sqrt{12(0.35)(0.65)}\\approx1.65.\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "workedExampleCard",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example 4.2",
          "ar": null
        },
        "problem": {
          "en": "Weights are \\(N(68,\\,5^2)\\). Find \\(P(60\\le X\\le75).\\)",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p>GDC: <code>normalcdf</code>(60, 75, 68, 5) \\(\\approx0.868.\\)</p><p>Alternatively: \\(z_1=(60-68)/5=-1.6,\\;z_2=(75-68)/5=1.4.\\)</p><p>\\(P=\\Phi(1.4)-\\Phi(-1.6)=0.9192-0.0548=0.8644.\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Normal distribution",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( X\\sim N(\\mu,\\sigma^2) \\); use GDC <code>normalcdf</code>, <code>invNorm</code>",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Binomial distribution",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( X\\sim B(n,p) \\); \\( P(X=r)=\\binom{n}{r}p^r(1-p)^{n-r} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "warn",
        "label": {
          "en": "Practice Problem",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A bag contains 4 red and 6 blue balls. Two are drawn without replacement. Find P(both same colour).</p><details style=\"margin-top:8px\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;font-weight:600\">Show solution</summary><div style=\"margin-top:8px\"><p>\\(P(RR)=\\frac{4}{10}\\cdot\\frac{3}{9}=\\frac{12}{90},\\quadP(BB)=\\frac{6}{10}\\cdot\\frac{5}{9}=\\frac{30}{90}.\\)</p><p>\\(P(\\text{same})=\\frac{42}{90}=\\frac{7}{15}\\approx0.467.\\)</p></div></details>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example-grid",
        "label": {
          "en": "Normal distribution probability",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>\\(X\\sim N(50,\\,9^2)\\). Find \\(P(44 &lt; X &lt; 62)\\).</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong> Standardise: \\(z_1=\\dfrac{44-50}{9}\\approx-0.667\\), \\(z_2=\\dfrac{62-50}{9}\\approx1.333\\)</p><p>\\(P = \\Phi(1.333)-\\Phi(-0.667)\\approx0.9088-0.2525=0.656\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example-grid",
        "label": {
          "en": "Expected value and variance",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A discrete RV \\(X\\) takes values 1,2,3 with probabilities 0.2, 0.5, 0.3. Find \\(E(X)\\) and \\(\\text{Var}(X)\\).</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong> \\(E(X)=1(0.2)+2(0.5)+3(0.3)=2.1\\)</p><p>\\(E(X^2)=1(0.2)+4(0.5)+9(0.3)=4.9\\)</p><p>\\(\\text{Var}(X)=4.9-2.1^2=0.49\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "<strong>Practice:</strong> A Binomial RV \\(X\\sim B(12,\\,0.3)\\). Find \\(P(X=4)\\) and \\(E(X)\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(P(X=4)=\\binom{12}{4}(0.3)^4(0.7)^8\\approx0.2311\\).  \\(E(X)=np=12(0.3)=3.6\\)",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
